{"id":29016,"slug":"gummo","title":"Gummo","year":1997,"country":"United States","duration":89,"spine":1238,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/29016-gummo","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/ee80a634c0e634c52f798345fbfe84d1/rtrqKWGQibw8EKAsHq3rpJDM7jTV88_large.jpg","description":"Harmony Korine’s debut feature is an audacious, lyrical evocation of America’s rural underbelly, and an elegy in the southern-gothic tradition of William Faulkner and William Eggleston. Shot in Korine’s native Nashville—standing in for the tornado-ravaged Xenia, Ohio—the rough-hewn film follows two young friends, Tummler and Solomon, as they ride around town, huffing glue and hunting stray cats, their every local encounter charged with vaudevillian anarchy as well as deep pathos. At once transgressive and empathetic, disturbing and undeniably beautiful, Gummo is a one-of-a-kind portrait of angelic and devilish souls caught in a cultural void, circumscribed by poverty and the depleted, alienated spiritual life of late-twentieth-century America.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Harmony Korine","slug":"harmony-korine"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Jacob Reynolds","role":"Solomon","slug":"jacob-reynolds"},{"actor":"Jacob Sewell","role":"Bunny Boy","slug":"jacob-sewell"},{"actor":"Nick Sutton","role":"Tummler","slug":"nick-sutton"},{"actor":"Chloë Sevigny","role":"Dot","slug":"chloe-sevigny"},{"actor":"Darby Dougherty","role":"Darby","slug":"darby-dougherty"},{"actor":"Carisa Glucksman","role":"Helen","slug":"carisa-glucksman"},{"actor":"Max Perlich","role":"Cole","slug":"max-perlich"},{"actor":"Linda Manz","role":"Solomon’s mother","slug":"linda-manz"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Harmony Korine","slug":"harmony-korine"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Harmony Korine","slug":"harmony-korine"},{"role":"Director of photography","person":"Jean-Yves Escoffier","slug":null},{"role":"Casting by","person":"Lyn Richmond","slug":null},{"role":"Music supervisor